# Adding screens

## Authenticated app screens

Create `src/app/(app)/<route>/page.tsx`. Every screen is wrapped in
`TalvoFrame` (the app shell: navigation, header, ⌘K), with the page's nav
index, and composed of the section blocks in `src/components/studio/blocks.tsx`
laid out with `Columns` from `src/components/studio/frames.tsx`.

Skeleton:

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from "next";

import { TalvoFrame } from "@/components/app/talvo";
import { Bare, Columns } from "@/components/studio/frames";
import { DataTableCard, PageHeaderBlock, StatRow } from "@/components/studio/blocks";

export const metadata: Metadata = { title: "Screen name" };

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <TalvoFrame current={7}>
      <Bare>
        <PageHeaderBlock title="Screen name" description="What it's for" primaryAction="Primary action" />
      </Bare>
      <StatRow stats={[/* … */]} />
      <Columns>{/* two blocks side by side */}</Columns>
    </TalvoFrame>
  );
}
```

Then register it: add its name to `NAV` and its route to `LINKS` in
`src/components/app/talvo.tsx` (in the same position; `current` is that
index), and add the route to the protected routes in `src/proxy.ts`.

## Patterns by screen type

- **List screen** → `FilterBarBlock` + `DataTableCard` (see `/payments`)
- **Overview** → `StatRow`, charts and lists in `Columns` (see `/dashboard`)
- **Time** → `ScheduleCard` or a calendar (see `/calendar`)
- **Pipeline** → `BoardBlock` (see `/deals`)
- **Settings** → tabs in the page header with `OnTab` sections (see `/settings`)
- **Auth** → `src/app/(auth)/<route>/page.tsx`; the layout centers a card

## Data

Content is the blocks' props, written in the page file. To show real data,
load it in the page (a server component) and pass it in; the database is
Prisma (`prisma/schema.prisma`, `src/lib/db.ts`).
